{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-08 11:11:08 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-DocsJson] [Project: doc_registration_fix] Found the root cause and existing spec! docs_json is initialized in set_project (lines 251-256 in set_project.py) with structure {architecture, phase_plan, checklist, progress_log}. The column exists in database (confirmed in upsert_project line 60-66 in sqlite.py). Problem: auto-created docs (research, bug reports) are NOT added to docs_json after creation.\", <parameter name=\"status\">success | findings=[\"docs_json is JSON dict with keys: architecture, phase_plan, checklist, progress_log\", \"initialized in set_project.py lines 251-256\", \"persisted to DB in upsert_project at line 295\", \"storage/sqlite.py has update_project_docs method at line 177\", \"spec SPEC-MANAGE-DOCS-001 documents the complete registration flow needed\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Searched set_project.py for docs_json initialization and found it in project_data dict around line 251\", \"what\": \"docs_json is a JSON object mapping doc types to file paths. Standard docs are registered in set_project at lines 251-256. Need to find if auto-created docs call update_project_docs\", \"why\": \"Understanding what structure docs_json has and where it gets initialized is critical for finding the gap in auto-doc registration\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/doc_registration_fix/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T11:11:08.552272+00:00_15aea078", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T11:11:08.552304+00:00"}
